+## States
+
+### State Matrix
+
+| State | Preheat | Home | Jog | Section Visibility |
+|-------|---------|------|-----|-------------------|
+| **Idle** (online, not printing) | Enabled | Enabled | Enabled | Visible |
+| **Pending** (action in flight) | Spinner + dim | Spinner + dim | Spinner + dim | Visible |
+| **Printing / Paused** | Disabled | Disabled | Disabled | Visible |
+| **Offline** | — | — | — | **Hidden** |
+| **Capability missing** | See below | See below | See below | Partial |
+
+### Capability-Gated Subgroups
+
+When a printer lacks a specific capability, **hide the entire subgroup** rather than rendering disabled rows. This avoids visual clutter and confusion for printers that will never support certain features.
+
+| Capability Flag | Subgroup Affected | Behavior When `false` |
+|-----------------|-------------------|----------------------|
+| `supportsTemperatureControl` | Preheat | **Hide entire Preheat subgroup** |
+| `supportsMovement` | Home, Jog | **Hide entire Home and Jog subgroups** |
+
+**Implementation:**
+
+```swift
+// In controlsSection(printer:)
+if printer.capabilities.supportsTemperatureControl {
+    PreheatSubgroup(printer: printer, viewModel: viewModel)
+}
+
+if printer.capabilities.supportsMovement {
+    HomeSubgroup(printer: printer, viewModel: viewModel)
+    JogSubgroup(printer: printer, viewModel: viewModel)
+}
+```
+
+**Rationale:** Hiding is cleaner UX than disabled-row clutter. Users should only see controls their printer can actually use. This is distinct from the "disabled during print" state, which shows controls but blocks interaction.
+
+### Idle State
+
+- All controls interactive
+- Standard color tokens (`pfCard`, `pfAccent`, `pfTextPrimary`)
+
+### Pending State
+
+When an action is in flight (e.g., waiting for backend response):
+
+```swift
+// PreheatRow with pending state
+HStack {
+    if isPending {
+        ProgressView()
+            .frame(width: 24, height: 24)
+    } else {
+        Image(systemName: icon)
+            .frame(width: 24)
+    }
+    
+    Text(materialName)
+        .foregroundStyle(isPending ? Color.pfTextTertiary : Color.pfTextPrimary)
+    
+    Spacer()
+    
+    Text(tempLabel)
+        .foregroundStyle(Color.pfTextTertiary)
+}
+.opacity(isPending ? 0.6 : 1.0)
+.disabled(isPending)
+```
+
+**Pending visual treatment:**
+- Replace icon with `ProgressView()` spinner
+- Opacity: `0.6`
+- Text color: `pfTextTertiary`
+- Interaction: disabled
+
+### Disabled-While-Printing State
+
+When `printer.state ∈ {Printing, Pausing, Paused, Resuming, Cancelling, Heating}`:
+
+```swift
+// DisabledControlRow
+HStack {
+    Image(systemName: icon)
+        .foregroundStyle(Color.pfTextTertiary)
+        .frame(width: 24)
+    
+    Text(label)
+        .foregroundStyle(Color.pfTextTertiary)
+    
+    Spacer()
+    
+    // Add lock icon for color-blind accessibility
+    Image(systemName: "lock.fill")
+        .font(.caption2)
+        .foregroundStyle(Color.pfTextTertiary)
+}
+.opacity(0.5)
+.disabled(true)
+```
+
+**Disabled visual treatment (color-blind friendly):**
+- Opacity: `0.5`
+- Text/icon color: `pfTextTertiary`
+- **Lock icon:** Small `lock.fill` at trailing edge — provides non-color indicator
+- No interaction
+
+### Hidden-While-Offline State
+
+The entire Controls section is conditionally rendered:
+
+```swift
+// In printerContent(_:)
+if printer.isOnline {
+    controlsSection(printer)
+}
+```
+
+When `printer.isOnline == false`, the section does not render at all.
